@startuml
' Parallel diagnosis model — English rendering.
'
' Language pairing (2026-09-04): every diagram on the page
' clinical-genetic-diagnosis-guide exists twice. This file is the ENGLISH one
' and keeps the base name, because the IG's default language is English
' (i18n-default-lang: en); the German twin is diagnose-parallelmodell-de.puml
' and renders to …-de.svg. Until 2026-09-04 a single German diagram served both
' trees, so English readers were shown German labels — and its labels were
' ASCII-transliterated ("Phaenotyp"), which is simply wrong German.
' Keep the two files in step: a change to one belongs in the other.
skinparam backgroundColor transparent
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam roundcorner 8
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam ArrowColor #555555
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #4a86e8
  BackgroundColor #eef4fd
  FontColor #1a1a1a
}

title Parallel diagnosis model — suspected, clinical, genetic

rectangle "**Suspected diagnosis**\n<size:11>Condition</size>\n<size:11>verificationStatus = **provisional**</size>\n<size:11>category = encounter-diagnosis</size>" as V #fff8e1
rectangle "**Clinical diagnosis**\n<size:11>MII_PR_Seltene_ClinicalDiagnosis</size>\n<size:11>verificationStatus = **confirmed**</size>\n<size:11>category = encounter-diagnosis</size>\n<size:11>evidence → HPO observations</size>" as K #e8f5e9
rectangle "**Genetic diagnosis**\n<size:11>MII_PR_Seltene_GeneticDiagnosis</size>\n<size:11>verificationStatus = **confirmed**</size>\n<size:11>category = SCT#782964007 Genetic disease</size>\n<size:11>evidence → MolGen variant</size>" as G #e3f2fd

V -down-> K : phenotypic\nwork-up
K -right-> G : molecular\nconfirmation

note bottom of K
  **Both exist side by side.**
  The genetic diagnosis does NOT replace
  the clinical one — it complements it.
  A patient ends up carrying two
  Condition resources.
end note

@enduml
